GitHub Pages runs Jekyll over a site by default, and Jekyll skips every
file and directory whose name starts with an underscore. This empty file
turns that off, so the directory is published exactly as it is committed.

It matters here even though no current filename starts with an
underscore: the day somebody adds one, the file would vanish from the
published site with no error anywhere, and the build would still be
green. Removing this file is how that happens.
